ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: consolidation.seq.sleep
display_id: SEQ-CONSOLIDATION-SLEEP
module: consolidation
title: Sleep run
summary: >-
  While the agent is idle, turns new experience into the memories its emotion calls for, then
  sweeps retention and refreshes the index.
notes: >-
  A run appraises new experience, judges the most salient episodes, replays them into memories,
  and processes raw captures before the sweep and index refresh.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: The scheduler starts a sleep run for a stack
participants:
  - id: core
    is:
      - sys.daemon
    label: Sleep run
  - id: db
    is:
      - sys.home
    label: Stack database
  - sys.model
items: []
parts:
  - consolidation.seq.sleep.a
  - consolidation.seq.sleep.b
  - consolidation.seq.sleep.c
rationale: >-
  Appraisal and judging come before replay selection so replay ranks episodes by their best
  available appraisal. Partial progress is kept: every applied change commits on its own, and
  a failure leaves unprocessed episodes pending for the next run.


  The run pauses when the day's allowance is spent instead of switching to cheaper extraction,
  so pending episodes keep their priority and resume the next day.
